# R8 keep rules. AGP merges every file in src/main/keepRules and passes it to R8.
#
# The release build currently runs WITHOUT R8 (see the `optimization { }` block in
# app/build.gradle.kts), so nothing below is active yet. These are the rules that have to be in
# place at the moment it is switched on:
#
#     Release builds are not exercised on a device in this repository. Turning R8 on changes the
#     one artifact users actually install, so enable it together with these rules and smoke-test
#     the release build — at minimum: launch it, solve 1, 2, 3, 4, and open the result screen.
#
# The two screens are referenced by *name* in res/navigation/nav_graph.xml, and Navigation
# instantiates them reflectively. R8 cannot see that reference, so without these rules a fragment
# can be renamed or removed and the app crashes as soon as it navigates.

-keep class com.a24solver.wakusei.FirstFragment { <init>(); }
-keep class com.a24solver.wakusei.SecondFragment { <init>(); }

# The solver package is reached through FirstFragment, so ordinary reachability keeps it and no
# rules are needed. It uses java.math.BigInteger and the Kotlin stdlib only, which ship their own
# rules with the Android plugin.
